        "title": "Image Processing: Geometric Correction, Atmospheric Correction, Classification",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "An EO image is a measurement of electromagnetic energy, distorted by the sensor optics, the satellite's position and attitude, the atmosphere, and terrain geometry. Image processing removes these distortions and extracts thematic information. The pipeline is always: geometric -> radiometric -> thematic."
    },
